  "limitations": [
    "Every body from the init/probe down to the SPI read/write callbacks executes in the sensor-hub emulator; only the SPI transfer helper 0x80f898ae, memcpy, the delay and the logger are supplied. The spi stub captures the transmitted bytes and injects authored receive bytes and statuses; no transfer reaches a real bus or LSM6DSO.",
    "The SPI handle word 0x80f17018 is .bss set at runtime by the caller 0x80f726ee; its value here is authored. The bus instance, chip select, SPI mode, clock and the helper internals are not executed.",
    "A failed CTRL3_C read during the reset poll makes the original accessor read an uninitialized stack byte; vectors do not exercise that path. A failed WHO_AM_I read leaves the caller buffer unchanged, so the cached id is the previous attempt value (zero before the first good read).",
    "Configuration beyond reset/identity (ODR, full scale, FIFO, interrupt routing, embedded functions), reset timing and the fitted part remain unproved and need the device. This is a probe and bus-framing contract, not a working IMU driver."
  ],
